#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
gdrive-od-ui — tray icon and window for gdrive-od (Google Drive on demand for KDE).

  * Tray icon: up to date / syncing / needs attention / not running, with quick actions.
  * Accounts: every account and section (My Drive, Shared with me, each Shared drive) with its
    state, last sync, file counts and change-feed health; Sync now, Open, Reconnect, Start/Stop.
  * Backup: live progress (files, bytes, speed, time left), folders to back up, pause/resume.
  * Activity: recent uploads, downloads, deletions, conflicts and refusals.
  * Settings: sections, Shared drives, Shared with me, check intervals, start at login.

The sync services don't need this app. It reads their status files
(~/.local/state/gdrive-ondemand/<account>.status.json) and acts through the gdrive-od command,
the config file and the systemd user units, reusing gdrive-od's own code.
Needs PySide6 (Arch: pyside6).
"""
